`p2` has the same compiler options whichever project was opened first, with `strict` set, as `tsc -p p2 --showConfig` reports.

**Impact:** in a repository with a circular `extends` chain, a project that extends into the cycle can get the wrong compiler options and config file list on the API, depending on which project was opened first, with no error beyond the TS18000 that `tsc -p` also reports, so an analyzer reads that project with options `tsc -p` does not use.

Opening `p1` parses `base.json` and then `a.json` through the extended config cache with `base.json` on the resolution stack, so [`getExtendedConfig` parses `base.json` without the cache](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/042e0fb9574980bd67964165df295e629f834fe3/tsc/internal/tsoptions/tsconfigparsing.go#L947-L951) and `parseConfig` stops there with TS18000. The cached `a.json` entry therefore has none of what `base.json` brings in: neither `strict` nor `strict.json`. Opening `p2` loads `a.json` with only `p2/tsconfig.json` on the stack, where a fresh parse follows `base.json` and `strict.json`, but [the cache entry's hash](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/042e0fb9574980bd67964165df295e629f834fe3/tsc/internal/project/extendedconfigcache.go#L41-L52) covers only the file contents, which are unchanged, so [`isExpired`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/042e0fb9574980bd67964165df295e629f834fe3/tsc/internal/project/extendedconfigcache.go#L35-L37) returns false and `p2` gets the entry built under `p1`'s stack.

`tsc -b` loses options the same way, because [its own extended config cache](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/042e0fb9574980bd67964165df295e629f834fe3/tsc/internal/execute/tsc/extendedconfigcache.go#L28-L35) also keys entries by path alone. With `"compilerOptions": { "noUnusedLocals": true }` added to `a.json` and an unused local in `p1`, `tsc -b p1 p2 --singleThreaded` reports no TS6133 for `p1` in 3 of 3 runs, while `tsc -b p1 --singleThreaded` and `tsc -p p1` report it. Without `--singleThreaded` the same build hangs, which is #64833.

